# PQC Triage runs with zero required environment variables.
#
# Local development (and `npm test`) use the embedded PGlite adapter by default,
# so you never need to fill this file in. Everything below is production-only.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` only if you want to point a local build at a hosted store.

# --- Production persistence -------------------------------------------------
# A pooled Postgres connection string. On Vercel, install the Neon integration
# and this variable is injected for you. Locally, leave it unset to use PGlite.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/db?sslmode=require

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Overrides the PGlite data directory for local development.
# PGLITE_DATA_DIR=.pgdata

# Public base URL of the deployment. Used for canonical URLs, the sitemap,
# OpenGraph metadata, the README badge, and public/mcp.json. Optional: the app
# derives it from the incoming request when unset.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-alias.vercel.app